This product bundles a modified copy of the `daam` Python package
(https://github.com/castorini/daam, MIT License, Copyright (c) 2022
Castorini, author Raphael Tang) under the `daam/` directory.

Modifications to the upstream v0.0.12 include, but are not limited to:

  * `daam/heatmap.py`
      - added `crop_heat_map_bbox(...)` — BFS-based island extraction that
        turns a continuous heat map into a list of pseudo bounding boxes
        (x1, y1, x2, y2);
      - added `return_overlay_heat_map(...)` and modified
        `WordHeatMap.plot_overlay(...)` so the call returns
        `(image, resized_heat_map, bbox_list)` instead of only drawing with
        matplotlib;
      - added a required `src_size` parameter so the overlay can be scaled
        back to the original (pre-resize) image dimensions;
      - added `visualize_tool(...)` helper.

  * `daam/trace.py`
      - added `search_closest_factor(x)` and use it in `_unravel_attn` to
        support non-square latent grids (e.g. 96x96 for 768-px inputs);
      - `latent_hw` is now selected between 4096 and 9216 based on the
        pipeline's sample size.

See `docs/modifications.md` for the full diff summary and rationale.

The demo script `demo_daam.py` at the repository root was written for
this project and is released under the same MIT License.
